.TH tupatch n 0.23.0 tclutils "Tcl Library Procedures"
.SH NAME
tupatch \- Apply unified diffs in pure Tcl.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
.nf
package require tclutils::tupatch
.fi
.SH COMMANDS
.PP
.nf
::tclutils::tupatch::parse patchText
::tclutils::tupatch::text sourceText patchText ?options?
::tclutils::tupatch::fromFile sourceFile patchText ?options?
.fi
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
.nf
\-reverse 0|1        apply patch in reverse, default 0
\-strict 0|1         verify context and removed lines, default 1
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
BtupatchR applies unified diffs and is the counterpart to
Btclutils::tudiffR. It supports full-file hunks generated by
BtudiffR and generic multi-hunk unified diffs with B@@R hunk headers.
.PP
The command BparseR returns a list of hunk dictionaries. Each hunk has
BoldStartR, BoldLenR, BnewStartR, BnewLenR, and BbodyR keys.
The body is a list of two-element records Ikind contentR where kind is one
of space, plus, or minus.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.nf
set patch [::tclutils::tudiff::unifiedText $old $new]
set result [::tclutils::tupatch::text $old $patch]
.fi
.PP
.nf
set reverted [::tclutils::tupatch::text $new $patch \-reverse 1]
.fi
.SH ERRORS
.PP
.nf
TCLUTILS TUPATCH CONTEXT   context or deleted line does not match
TCLUTILS TUPATCH RANGE     hunk is outside the source or overlaps
.fi
.SH LIMITATIONS
.PP
The line model follows Btclutils::common::splitLinesR and joins output with
newline characters. Special external patch details such as
BNo newline at end of fileR are ignored.
.SH SEE ALSO
tclutils(n), tudiff(n)
